Files that trx64u.cor installs into its core folder (record 8 of the .cor, tools/cor_pack.py; the pin's FILES=). The application writes each one that is missing
to <core folder>/<path> at the start and never overwrites one (coreapp/src/instfiles.cc).

sidplayer/sidcrt.bin, muscrt.bin, musplayer.bin: the C64 programs of the SID player - the cartridge programs for .sid and .mus/.str and the MUS player that is
copied to $E000. They are the files TRX64-Ultimate's firmware plays tunes with, byte for byte (software/ultimate-app/software/6502/sidcrt/target/*.bin, built
there by 64tass from sidcrt.asm, muscrt.asm, musplayer.asm; source commit f0c51d11 of that tree). Author: Wilfred Bos / Gideon Zweijtzer, copyright
2009-2023, GPL-3.0 (the licence of TRX64-Ultimate and of this repository). sha256:
  34f37d9388ef987fb30b24dbec7bb6dfb628a4e892396996a722ce8266b4287f  sidplayer/sidcrt.bin
  18aef177afc8d80806aa874ee18952249ab5b41fcc9bada7d1178d334e5187b5  sidplayer/muscrt.bin
  92bb91eb94556efa404a5af03104cc387851c7c7080e3238bba477b50db66999  sidplayer/musplayer.bin
They hold no Commodore ROM: the 16 KB cartridge image is made at play time from sidcrt.bin (8 KB) and the BASIC ROM the machine runs with.

modplayer/module.bin: the 16 KB MOD player cartridge image that "Play MOD" starts, byte for byte TRX64-Ultimate's software/ModPlayer_16k/module.bin (that
firmware links it into its application, target/u2/zpu/ultimate/Makefile:156 SRCS_BIN). It carries no licence header; TRX64-Ultimate's GitHub export treats it
as third-party content at Gideon's path and leaves it out (tools/gh_export.py:61), and tools/github_snapshot.py leaves it out here too. sha256:
  fa1484bdd494c83cfe6436febde768b2c368f1ed0af7837b6a8c06fde96af038  modplayer/module.bin
